WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
[Music]

2
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.800
Hermes took over my TV.

3
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:04.800
A 58" Roku TV, controlled over Wi-Fi.
No app. No dev mode. Roku's own local API.

4
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.200
It finds the TV by itself.

5
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.900
It asks the network first, then scans
for Roku's control port, 8060.

6
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.600
It knows every app.

7
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.400
Every app and input on the TV, with the
ID it uses to open each one.

8
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.200
42 apps and inputs on my TV: Netflix,
YouTube, Hulu, Disney Plus and more

9
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.500
Ask it in plain words.

10
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.200
"Put the Tesla livestream on the TV."

11
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.900
Illustration. The tool behind it
played this on my TV on Oct 18.

12
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.000
How it plays the exact video.

13
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.600
It looks up the video, then tells the
TV's YouTube app which one to open.

14
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.000
1 yt-dlp finds the video ID
2 POST launch  3 It plays on the TV

15
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.200
A remote, from the chat.

16
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:31.000
Home, Play, Back, volume, power,
typing into search boxes.

17
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.000
What it can't do.

18
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.700
Remove ads: no. Hide home rows: no.
Install apps: only in Roku dev mode.

19
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.400
Needs: same Wi-Fi, port 8060 open.

20
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.600
My TV. One skill.
$ ~/hermes-roku/roku.py find

21
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.600
Real output from my TV. Tested by me
Oct 18. The TV screen is an illustration.

22
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:41.800
[Music fades out]
